1
00:00:01,784 --> 00:00:05,440
[bright flute music]

2
00:00:05,570 --> 00:00:07,877
- [Hiraku Voiceover] Let me tell
you a story about a slime.

3
00:00:08,008 --> 00:00:09,705
One day, the slime that
Tia brought here to

4
00:00:09,835 --> 00:00:13,187
purify our waste water and
sewage started to multiply

5
00:00:13,317 --> 00:00:16,103
and now there are lots of
different types of slimes.

6
00:00:16,233 --> 00:00:17,626
They were all harmless,

7
00:00:17,756 --> 00:00:18,931
so I didn't really notice that

8
00:00:19,062 --> 00:00:21,630
they'd been multiplying, but...

9
00:00:21,760 --> 00:00:23,284
[girls gasping]

10
00:00:23,414 --> 00:00:26,026
[dramatic music]

11
00:00:26,156 --> 00:00:27,679
[slime farting]

12
00:00:27,810 --> 00:00:28,985
[slime babbling]

13
00:00:29,116 --> 00:00:30,813
- [Tia] Did it drink
an entire barrel?

14
00:00:30,943 --> 00:00:32,641
- A single slime drank it all?

15
00:00:32,771 --> 00:00:35,122
- My dad can only drink
half a barrel at most.

16
00:00:35,252 --> 00:00:37,124
- That wine was
everyone's property!

17
00:00:37,254 --> 00:00:39,213
- [Lastismoon] You can't go and
drink it without our permission!

18
00:00:39,343 --> 00:00:40,736
- This deserves punishment!

19
00:00:40,866 --> 00:00:42,390
- [Tia] That's right!
- [Lastismoon] Yeah!

20
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:44,000
- [Sena] Please wait
a minute, everyone!

21
00:00:44,131 --> 00:00:46,046
Let's all calm down!

22
00:00:46,176 --> 00:00:47,395
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
This came as a big shock

23
00:00:47,525 --> 00:00:49,440
to all the alcohol-loving
residents here.

24
00:00:49,571 --> 00:00:52,530
And so began our
village's first trial.

25
00:00:52,661 --> 00:00:54,663
[slime babbling]

26
00:00:56,839 --> 00:00:58,188
- Wait! Let's not!

27
00:00:58,319 --> 00:00:59,668
- Leave it to me!
- Guilty.

28
00:00:59,798 --> 00:01:00,669
- But, Anne!

29
00:01:00,799 --> 00:01:01,974
Oh dear!

30
00:01:02,105 --> 00:01:03,585
- Wait!
- Are we blowing something up?

31
00:01:03,715 --> 00:01:05,108
- I feel bad for it,

32
00:01:05,239 --> 00:01:07,415
so let's move away from
the barbaric options.

33
00:01:07,545 --> 00:01:09,634
How about short
confinement instead?

34
00:01:09,765 --> 00:01:11,723
- [Tia] But that was our
precious alcohol!

35
00:01:11,854 --> 00:01:13,116
[slime farting]

36
00:01:13,247 --> 00:01:14,422
- [Tia] Jeez, this kind
of stuff happens

37
00:01:14,552 --> 00:01:15,379
because you're too soft!

38
00:01:15,510 --> 00:01:16,685
- Pardon?

39
00:01:16,815 --> 00:01:18,948
We're talking about
a slime here.

40
00:01:19,079 --> 00:01:20,471
Even if we punish it,

41
00:01:20,602 --> 00:01:22,908
I'm not sure it's going to
reflect on its action.

42
00:01:23,039 --> 00:01:25,172
- [Tia] Well, you have a point.

43
00:01:25,302 --> 00:01:27,130
- [Lastismoon] It is
a slime, after all.

44
00:01:27,261 --> 00:01:30,307
- [Hiraku Voiceover] And so,
that slime was acquitted.

45
00:01:30,438 --> 00:01:32,701
After that, it began to
pop up during our feasts

46
00:01:32,831 --> 00:01:36,748
and celebrations so that
it could join us.

47
00:01:36,879 --> 00:01:40,361
Oh well. I think it's all right
if we have one slime like that.

48
00:01:40,491 --> 00:01:42,667
Too many would be
a problem, though.

49
00:01:44,191 --> 00:01:47,324
["Flower Ring" by Shino Shimoji
and Aya Suzaki plays]

50
00:03:13,628 --> 00:03:16,544
[bright violin music]

51
00:03:16,674 --> 00:03:18,676
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
The season is autumn.

52
00:03:18,807 --> 00:03:21,897
The summers here aren't
particularly hot or anything,

53
00:03:22,027 --> 00:03:23,594
but it's still nice when
things cool down a bit

54
00:03:23,725 --> 00:03:25,596
and we can get some
more work done.

55
00:03:25,727 --> 00:03:27,294
And here's the result.

56
00:03:27,424 --> 00:03:28,991
[stomach growling]

57
00:03:29,121 --> 00:03:30,340
- I'm so hungry.

58
00:03:30,471 --> 00:03:32,255
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
Autumn means eating.

59
00:03:32,386 --> 00:03:33,909
[Flowrem giggling]

60
00:03:34,039 --> 00:03:35,824
- [Flowrem] There's nothing
like a good hot pot!

61
00:03:35,954 --> 00:03:37,304
It's so tasty!

62
00:03:37,434 --> 00:03:39,131
- Would you stop taking
all the meat, Lasty?

63
00:03:39,262 --> 00:03:41,177
- I'm eating vegetables, too!

64
00:03:41,308 --> 00:03:42,613
[Sena slurping]

65
00:03:42,744 --> 00:03:43,919
- Yummy!

66
00:03:44,049 --> 00:03:46,138
We didn't have these
types of mushrooms

67
00:03:46,269 --> 00:03:47,662
in Howling Village.

68
00:03:47,792 --> 00:03:51,056
- Man, I really love
a good hot pot.

69
00:03:51,187 --> 00:03:52,667
If we could get seafood here,

70
00:03:52,797 --> 00:03:54,712
I bet these would taste
even better.

71
00:03:54,843 --> 00:03:56,192
[girls gasping]

72
00:03:56,323 --> 00:03:59,195
- So what exactly
are you referring to

73
00:03:59,326 --> 00:04:00,544
when you say seafood?

74
00:04:00,675 --> 00:04:02,242
- Let's see.

75
00:04:02,372 --> 00:04:05,201
Stuff like cod, crabs,
or monkfish.

76
00:04:05,332 --> 00:04:07,116
We can make broth from kombu!

77
00:04:07,247 --> 00:04:10,467
Then make a chanco miso hotpot!

78
00:04:10,598 --> 00:04:12,077
- Start researching immediately!

79
00:04:12,208 --> 00:04:13,557
- I've got some info here!

80
00:04:13,688 --> 00:04:14,515
- Oh no!

81
00:04:14,645 --> 00:04:15,646
What do I do?

82
00:04:15,777 --> 00:04:17,039
I've never even seen the ocean.

83
00:04:17,169 --> 00:04:18,519
- Did you say crabs?

84
00:04:18,649 --> 00:04:20,434
Can you eat those?

85
00:04:20,564 --> 00:04:22,131
They're really hard.

86
00:04:22,262 --> 00:04:23,480
- Kombu.

87
00:04:23,611 --> 00:04:25,656
It sounds like something
quite terrifying.

88
00:04:25,787 --> 00:04:26,527
[kombu growling]

89
00:04:26,657 --> 00:04:27,876
- A broth?

90
00:04:28,006 --> 00:04:29,269
That's the soup thing
you showed me

91
00:04:29,399 --> 00:04:30,748
how to make earlier, right?

92
00:04:30,879 --> 00:04:31,967
- That's right.

93
00:04:32,097 --> 00:04:33,795
- Is chanco a kind
of fish, then?

94
00:04:33,925 --> 00:04:35,492
- If we need the ocean,

95
00:04:35,623 --> 00:04:37,929
there's a port city
within the Demonic Kingdom.

96
00:04:38,060 --> 00:04:39,453
You're able to reach it

97
00:04:39,583 --> 00:04:41,846
if you head south
from this village.

98
00:04:41,977 --> 00:04:44,284
They do a lot of trading
of ocean products,

99
00:04:44,414 --> 00:04:46,938
so we might be able to find
some of those fish there.

100
00:04:47,069 --> 00:04:49,201
- Okay! I'll fly over
and check it out.

101
00:04:49,332 --> 00:04:50,115
- Wonderful.

102
00:04:50,246 --> 00:04:51,378
I can go with you.

103
00:04:51,508 --> 00:04:53,423
We can ask a merchant
I know for help.

104
00:04:53,554 --> 00:04:54,816
- [Lu] Let's get started
right away!

105
00:04:54,946 --> 00:04:56,948
- [Flora] I'll take care
of the miso!

106
00:04:58,907 --> 00:05:01,388
- They all really like
hotpots, huh?

107
00:05:02,127 --> 00:05:04,129
- [Anne] Indeed.

108
00:05:04,260 --> 00:05:05,217
- [Lastismoon] See you later!

109
00:05:05,348 --> 00:05:07,350
- [Lu] We're counting on you!

110
00:05:07,481 --> 00:05:08,612
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
When it comes to food,

111
00:05:08,743 --> 00:05:11,136
everyone here
gets very motivated.

112
00:05:11,267 --> 00:05:13,356
Well, nothing makes me
happier as a farmer

113
00:05:13,487 --> 00:05:15,880
than seeing them enjoy my food.

114
00:05:16,011 --> 00:05:17,926
[magical music]

115
00:05:18,056 --> 00:05:19,754
And so, the return of the group

116
00:05:19,884 --> 00:05:21,799
that set out in earnest
took place.

117
00:05:21,930 --> 00:05:23,888
Three days later.

118
00:05:24,019 --> 00:05:25,934
- It's a great pleasure
to meet everyone.

119
00:05:26,064 --> 00:05:27,109
My name is Michael.

120
00:05:27,239 --> 00:05:28,502
I'm an established merchant from

121
00:05:28,632 --> 00:05:31,418
the city of Shashato
in the Demonic Kingdom.

122
00:05:31,548 --> 00:05:33,158
- I'm the mayor, Hiraku.

123
00:05:33,289 --> 00:05:35,813
Thank you for coming here
to our little village.

124
00:05:35,944 --> 00:05:36,988
- Of course.

125
00:05:37,119 --> 00:05:38,338
It's nothing, really.

126
00:05:38,468 --> 00:05:40,296
This is part of my job
as a merchant.

127
00:05:40,427 --> 00:05:41,558
[group gasping]

128
00:05:41,689 --> 00:05:43,168
These are the marine
products I brought

129
00:05:43,299 --> 00:05:44,561
from the city of Shashato.

130
00:05:44,692 --> 00:05:46,302
They are our pride and joy.

131
00:05:46,433 --> 00:05:49,087
As for the seaweed called kombu
that you requested,

132
00:05:49,218 --> 00:05:50,741
our fishermen normally
throw it back,

133
00:05:50,872 --> 00:05:52,961
even if they pull up some
in their nets.

134
00:05:53,091 --> 00:05:54,571
- What? So...

135
00:05:54,702 --> 00:05:56,356
- No need to worry
about it, though.

136
00:05:56,486 --> 00:05:59,533
I'll have my men collect some
kombu for you right away.

137
00:05:59,663 --> 00:06:02,579
We'll have it dried and ready
before you know it.

138
00:06:02,710 --> 00:06:04,451
- That sounds great.

139
00:06:04,581 --> 00:06:07,932
- Now with regards to my visit
here to your village today,

140
00:06:08,063 --> 00:06:10,108
I have three main goals.

141
00:06:10,239 --> 00:06:11,283
[Hiraku sighing]

142
00:06:11,414 --> 00:06:13,198
The first is to
properly greet you

143
00:06:13,329 --> 00:06:14,678
and show you
my gratitude for

144
00:06:14,809 --> 00:06:16,854
requesting to do
business with us.

145
00:06:16,985 --> 00:06:19,466
The second is to suggest
more opportunities

146
00:06:19,596 --> 00:06:22,033
for us to trade goods
and do business.

147
00:06:22,730 --> 00:06:24,340
And my third goal,

148
00:06:24,471 --> 00:06:26,211
if it's something
you would agree to,

149
00:06:26,342 --> 00:06:28,344
is to become the official
government purveyor

150
00:06:28,475 --> 00:06:29,693
for this village.

151
00:06:29,824 --> 00:06:31,173
- Official purveyor?

152
00:06:31,303 --> 00:06:32,783
- It means he would
like to handle

153
00:06:32,914 --> 00:06:34,916
all trade between us
and the outside world.

154
00:06:35,046 --> 00:06:37,788
- You're being quite direct
in what you're asking for.

155
00:06:37,919 --> 00:06:39,616
- I'm always careful to not be

156
00:06:39,747 --> 00:06:42,576
so indirect that my intentions
are somehow misinterpreted.

157
00:06:42,706 --> 00:06:46,710
All of the crops here you
have are very enticing.

158
00:06:46,841 --> 00:06:49,757
If you allow me the
opportunity to do so,

159
00:06:49,887 --> 00:06:53,935
I can get you several times
more value when trading them.

160
00:06:56,111 --> 00:06:57,678
- There are quite a few
people already

161
00:06:57,808 --> 00:07:00,115
who want to do trade
with this village.

162
00:07:00,245 --> 00:07:03,074
- As I said, if you agree to it.

163
00:07:03,205 --> 00:07:05,250
Of course, I'd like to ask
that you first have

164
00:07:05,381 --> 00:07:06,643
a look at the
list of products

165
00:07:06,774 --> 00:07:08,776
that my company trades
for other entities.

166
00:07:08,906 --> 00:07:11,648
And from there, we can
discuss my proposition.

167
00:07:14,695 --> 00:07:16,131
I believe we were able to cover

168
00:07:16,261 --> 00:07:17,959
a lot of important ground today.

169
00:07:18,089 --> 00:07:19,569
Next time,
I'd like to discuss

170
00:07:19,700 --> 00:07:21,919
the alcohol produced
in this village.

171
00:07:22,050 --> 00:07:23,660
- [Lastismoon] You can't
have the alcohol!

172
00:07:23,791 --> 00:07:24,792
[Michael screaming]

173
00:07:24,922 --> 00:07:26,054
[Michael coughing]

174
00:07:26,184 --> 00:07:27,664
- Pardon my ignorance.

175
00:07:27,795 --> 00:07:29,884
I'll leave things as is now.

176
00:07:31,581 --> 00:07:33,801
- Well, he seemed like
a skilled merchant.

177
00:07:33,931 --> 00:07:35,411
That should come in handy.

178
00:07:35,542 --> 00:07:36,891
- It certainly will.

179
00:07:37,021 --> 00:07:39,023
- It'll be a big help
having him negotiate.

180
00:07:39,154 --> 00:07:41,025
- And even though he's
handling things for us,

181
00:07:41,156 --> 00:07:43,071
we'll get more goods
when trading now.

182
00:07:43,201 --> 00:07:46,553
- It doesn't seem like he has
any intention to deceive us.

183
00:07:46,683 --> 00:07:48,032
- Yeah.

184
00:07:48,163 --> 00:07:50,339
I hope our relationship
with him goes smoothly.

185
00:07:50,470 --> 00:07:52,167
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
It seemed like he was

186
00:07:52,297 --> 00:07:54,343
really frightened
there at the end.

187
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:56,040
But oh well.

188
00:07:56,171 --> 00:07:58,956
That's to be expected when
you're talking to a dragon.

189
00:07:59,087 --> 00:08:02,003
[ominous music]

190
00:08:04,571 --> 00:08:06,790
- [Michael] The Great
Tree Village, huh?

191
00:08:08,662 --> 00:08:10,490
[Michael sighing]

192
00:08:11,926 --> 00:08:14,319
[Michael screaming]

193
00:08:14,450 --> 00:08:16,278
- [Michael Voiceover]
That was scary!

194
00:08:16,408 --> 00:08:18,585
[upbeat electronic music]

195
00:08:20,021 --> 00:08:22,414
[seagulls squawking]
[playful music]

196
00:08:23,807 --> 00:08:25,156
- [Michael] A visitor?

197
00:08:25,287 --> 00:08:26,854
Without an appointment?

198
00:08:26,984 --> 00:08:29,726
- Yes. They would like to
talk business with you.

199
00:08:29,857 --> 00:08:32,120
- [Michael] I couldn't be
any busier now.

200
00:08:32,250 --> 00:08:35,253
- [Michael Voiceover]
My name is Michael Goroun.

201
00:08:35,384 --> 00:08:36,820
I work as the head of
the largest

202
00:08:36,951 --> 00:08:38,909
trading company
in this city.

203
00:08:39,040 --> 00:08:42,260
- If it's nothing major,
can't you guys handle it?

204
00:08:42,391 --> 00:08:45,089
Why do they need to
see me specifically?

205
00:08:45,220 --> 00:08:46,874
- The person that
requested you

206
00:08:47,004 --> 00:08:49,180
did so by name
when they arrived.

207
00:08:49,311 --> 00:08:51,139
They even brought goods
from their farm.

208
00:08:51,269 --> 00:08:53,184
I wasn't sure what to do.

209
00:08:53,315 --> 00:08:54,925
- They already brought
goods with them?

210
00:08:55,056 --> 00:08:56,448
Don't they know
the rules here?

211
00:08:56,579 --> 00:08:58,059
If you guys can't
handle it on your own,

212
00:08:58,189 --> 00:09:00,235
then just refer
them somewhere el-

213
00:09:02,411 --> 00:09:04,152
No, I'll meet with them.

214
00:09:04,935 --> 00:09:06,328
- Yes, sir.

215
00:09:06,458 --> 00:09:08,069
- [Michael Voiceover]
My merchant's intuition

216
00:09:08,199 --> 00:09:09,984
is telling me that
I can't ignore this.

217
00:09:10,114 --> 00:09:13,553
This strange feeling
welling up inside me is...

218
00:09:13,683 --> 00:09:17,687
- I feel so very honored
that you remember me still.

219
00:09:17,818 --> 00:09:19,123
- Yes, of course I do.

220
00:09:19,254 --> 00:09:20,516
If I remember correctly,

221
00:09:20,647 --> 00:09:22,431
the last time we had
the pleasure of meeting

222
00:09:22,562 --> 00:09:24,955
was at your birthday party.

223
00:09:25,086 --> 00:09:26,130
- [Michael Voiceover]
I can't believe the young lady

224
00:09:26,261 --> 00:09:27,654
of the Chrome family is here.

225
00:09:27,784 --> 00:09:30,613
My head would've rolled
if I had sent her away.

226
00:09:33,485 --> 00:09:34,835
- Who have you brought with you?

227
00:09:34,965 --> 00:09:36,880
- Oh! My companion is...

228
00:09:37,011 --> 00:09:39,622
- My name is Lastismoon
of the dragons.

229
00:09:39,753 --> 00:09:41,493
Please call me Lasty.

230
00:09:41,624 --> 00:09:43,408
- [Michael Voiceover]
Lastismoon?

231
00:09:43,539 --> 00:09:46,847
Could she really be
that crazy dragon?

232
00:09:46,977 --> 00:09:48,413
She's just a child!

233
00:09:48,544 --> 00:09:49,632
[Lastismoon sighing]

234
00:09:49,763 --> 00:09:51,155
The daughter of
one of the most

235
00:09:51,286 --> 00:09:53,244
powerful families of
the Demonic Kingdom

236
00:09:53,375 --> 00:09:55,029
and a dangerous dragon!

237
00:09:55,159 --> 00:09:57,814
The risks of trading
with them are too high.

238
00:09:57,945 --> 00:10:00,991
- So what is it that brings you
here to see me today?

239
00:10:01,122 --> 00:10:03,820
- [Michael Voiceover]
But I can't just ignore them!

240
00:10:05,169 --> 00:10:07,128
- We'd like you to
purchase these from us.

241
00:10:07,258 --> 00:10:08,608
[Michael gasping]

242
00:10:08,738 --> 00:10:09,957
And in exchange,
there are some things

243
00:10:10,087 --> 00:10:11,306
we'd like you to find.

244
00:10:11,436 --> 00:10:13,830
[Michael gasping]

245
00:10:13,961 --> 00:10:15,440
- [Michael Voiceover]
What's going on here?

246
00:10:15,571 --> 00:10:17,138
I'm being stared down
by a dragon

247
00:10:17,268 --> 00:10:18,966
while being surrounded
by lizardmen.

248
00:10:19,096 --> 00:10:22,491
I'm about to enter some
outrageous trade talks.

249
00:10:23,535 --> 00:10:24,885
Was that feeling I had before

250
00:10:25,015 --> 00:10:26,626
a warning of impending danger?

251
00:10:26,756 --> 00:10:28,453
[Michael inhaling]

252
00:10:29,585 --> 00:10:30,673
[Michael gasping]

253
00:10:30,804 --> 00:10:32,109
These are those fruit

254
00:10:32,240 --> 00:10:33,458
that have entered
the Demonic Kingdom

255
00:10:33,589 --> 00:10:35,156
that people have
been talking about!

256
00:10:35,286 --> 00:10:37,549
Each one of these can fetch
several silver coins!

257
00:10:37,680 --> 00:10:40,988
And look how many
they've brought!

258
00:10:41,118 --> 00:10:42,293
[coins rattling]

259
00:10:42,424 --> 00:10:43,686
- [Michael] The goods you wanted

260
00:10:43,817 --> 00:10:45,383
were from the ocean, correct?

261
00:10:45,514 --> 00:10:46,907
- That's right!

262
00:10:47,037 --> 00:10:49,387
- This port happens
to be my territory.

263
00:10:49,518 --> 00:10:52,129
I can find whatever it is
you are looking for.

264
00:10:52,260 --> 00:10:53,130
[girls gasping]

265
00:10:53,261 --> 00:10:54,523
Because that's...

266
00:10:54,654 --> 00:10:57,221
the job of a worthy
merchant like me!

267
00:10:57,352 --> 00:11:00,311
- [Michael Voiceover] I can't
let this chance get away.

268
00:11:00,442 --> 00:11:02,009
- I want you to go to the port

269
00:11:02,139 --> 00:11:03,488
and bring me their best catches!

270
00:11:03,619 --> 00:11:04,968
- Okay!

271
00:11:05,099 --> 00:11:06,622
- And after that, prepare
my things for travel!

272
00:11:06,753 --> 00:11:08,058
- [Employee] Yes, sir!

273
00:11:08,189 --> 00:11:10,321
- I'll take part in
the delivery myself.

274
00:11:10,452 --> 00:11:12,062
Are the goods
going to the capital?

275
00:11:12,193 --> 00:11:14,282
- Actually, they're
going to a village

276
00:11:14,412 --> 00:11:15,675
in The Forest of Death.

277
00:11:15,805 --> 00:11:17,067
- I'll carry the stuff,

278
00:11:17,198 --> 00:11:18,678
so I can give you
a ride as well.

279
00:11:18,808 --> 00:11:20,462
- [Michael Voiceover]
Forest of Death?

280
00:11:20,592 --> 00:11:22,116
Give me a ride?

281
00:11:23,900 --> 00:11:26,816
[Michael screaming]

282
00:11:28,775 --> 00:11:30,428
- He's a merchant from Shashato.

283
00:11:30,559 --> 00:11:31,429
- I see.

284
00:11:31,560 --> 00:11:33,083
[Michael screaming]

285
00:11:33,214 --> 00:11:34,345
- Oh.

286
00:11:34,476 --> 00:11:35,912
And the merchant came with you?

287
00:11:36,043 --> 00:11:39,089
[Michael growling]

288
00:11:39,220 --> 00:11:42,179
- [Michael Voiceover]
The mayor seems normal.

289
00:11:42,310 --> 00:11:43,659
[Michael gasping]

290
00:11:43,790 --> 00:11:45,226
- [Lastismoon] You can't
have the alcohol!

291
00:11:45,356 --> 00:11:48,229
[Michael trembling]

292
00:11:48,359 --> 00:11:51,145
[upbeat folk music]

293
00:11:53,060 --> 00:11:54,626
[Michael sighing]

294
00:11:54,757 --> 00:11:56,411
- [Michael Voiceover]
I survived it.

295
00:11:56,541 --> 00:11:59,283
I managed to finish my business
with that terrifying group

296
00:11:59,414 --> 00:12:01,155
while having a smile on my face.

297
00:12:01,285 --> 00:12:04,071
That was the best deal
of my life.

298
00:12:04,201 --> 00:12:06,813
Huge profits are waiting for me
from here on out.

299
00:12:06,943 --> 00:12:08,205
[Michael sighing]

300
00:12:08,336 --> 00:12:09,467
However...

301
00:12:09,598 --> 00:12:10,947
[stomach grumbling]

302
00:12:11,078 --> 00:12:12,557
[Michael groaning]

303
00:12:12,688 --> 00:12:15,517
I'm not sure if my body
can handle this.

304
00:12:19,608 --> 00:12:22,437
[girls gasping]

305
00:12:23,394 --> 00:12:24,744
[Hiraku humming]

306
00:12:24,874 --> 00:12:26,963
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
Here it is, real seafood!

307
00:12:27,094 --> 00:12:30,227
Maybe next time I'll ask him
for shrimp or squid!

308
00:12:30,358 --> 00:12:33,535
[girls giggling]

309
00:12:33,665 --> 00:12:36,712
[bright folk music]
[banging]

310
00:12:38,235 --> 00:12:39,976
[dragon growling]

311
00:12:40,107 --> 00:12:41,586
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
This is the third time a dragon

312
00:12:41,717 --> 00:12:43,414
has attacked this village.

313
00:12:43,545 --> 00:12:44,894
I think.

314
00:12:45,025 --> 00:12:47,941
Is this one related
to Dryme again?

315
00:12:48,071 --> 00:12:50,160
For the record,
the three angel squad

316
00:12:50,291 --> 00:12:51,901
in charge of
patrolling the skies

317
00:12:52,032 --> 00:12:53,685
was quickly able to
spot this dragon

318
00:12:53,816 --> 00:12:55,296
before it fully reached us.

319
00:12:55,426 --> 00:12:58,778
However, stopping a dragon
proved to be difficult.

320
00:12:58,908 --> 00:13:01,868
But seriously,
what is that dragon doing?

321
00:13:01,998 --> 00:13:04,348
Acting smug?

322
00:13:04,479 --> 00:13:05,915
[fireball exploding]

323
00:13:06,046 --> 00:13:08,309
[Hiraku groaning]

324
00:13:08,439 --> 00:13:10,224
Okay, so you're challenging me.

325
00:13:10,354 --> 00:13:11,791
You want a fight, right?

326
00:13:11,921 --> 00:13:13,705
In that case...

327
00:13:17,274 --> 00:13:18,493
I missed!

328
00:13:18,623 --> 00:13:20,538
Is what I want it to think.

329
00:13:20,669 --> 00:13:22,236
Once more!

330
00:13:23,237 --> 00:13:24,760
Defeated!

331
00:13:24,891 --> 00:13:26,414
[crash]

332
00:13:27,067 --> 00:13:28,808
[wolves barking]

333
00:13:28,938 --> 00:13:30,287
[Hiraku groaning]

334
00:13:30,418 --> 00:13:32,115
- Ow, ow, ow!

335
00:13:32,246 --> 00:13:34,552
Aw, you got me
with that spear.

336
00:13:34,683 --> 00:13:35,858
I surrender!

337
00:13:35,989 --> 00:13:37,468
Just kidding.
[chuckling]

338
00:13:37,599 --> 00:13:39,470
- Why'd you do
something like that?

339
00:13:39,601 --> 00:13:42,691
- Well, you see, it really isn't
all that big of an issue.

340
00:13:42,822 --> 00:13:44,649
- But you burned
some of the forest.

341
00:13:44,780 --> 00:13:46,434
- Okay. Give me a minute.

342
00:13:46,564 --> 00:13:48,610
I'll come up with an important
reason why I did that.

343
00:13:48,740 --> 00:13:49,785
[Hiraku growling]

344
00:13:49,916 --> 00:13:51,221
- Hey!

345
00:13:51,352 --> 00:13:55,486
Wait a minute, mayor!

346
00:13:55,617 --> 00:13:56,879
I'm sorry, mayor, she's...

347
00:13:57,010 --> 00:13:58,315
[Hakuren gasping]

348
00:13:58,446 --> 00:14:00,665
- It's little Drymey!
- [Hiraku] Little?

349
00:14:00,796 --> 00:14:03,190
- [Hiraku Voiceover] According
to Dryme's explanation,

350
00:14:03,320 --> 00:14:04,931
her name is Hakuren.

351
00:14:05,061 --> 00:14:07,150
She's his older sister.

352
00:14:07,281 --> 00:14:09,413
- This is your fault,
you know, Drymey.

353
00:14:09,544 --> 00:14:12,721
You said you were giving away
Lasty as a bride-to-be.

354
00:14:12,852 --> 00:14:13,896
- As a bride?

355
00:14:14,027 --> 00:14:14,941
- No, that's not what I-

356
00:14:15,071 --> 00:14:16,290
- You totally said that!

357
00:14:16,420 --> 00:14:17,987
You said you wanted
to marry her off

358
00:14:18,118 --> 00:14:19,815
to the mayor of
this village someday.

359
00:14:19,946 --> 00:14:20,860
- Wait, what?

360
00:14:20,990 --> 00:14:22,296
- It's not like that!

361
00:14:22,426 --> 00:14:24,167
I might've said something
kind of like that

362
00:14:24,298 --> 00:14:25,690
while I was drinking, but...

363
00:14:25,821 --> 00:14:26,866
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
As the person in question,

364
00:14:26,996 --> 00:14:28,606
it makes it hard to comment.

365
00:14:28,737 --> 00:14:30,347
- So that's why I came out here,

366
00:14:30,478 --> 00:14:32,915
to see what kind of person he
was marrying my niece off to!

367
00:14:33,046 --> 00:14:35,657
- Then why couldn't you just
come visit like normal?

368
00:14:35,787 --> 00:14:38,921
- Everyone always talks about
how strong the mayor here is.

369
00:14:39,052 --> 00:14:40,836
So I wanted to come
play with you a little.

370
00:14:40,967 --> 00:14:42,011
[Hiraku growling]

371
00:14:42,142 --> 00:14:43,621
- It's not just that, though.

372
00:14:43,752 --> 00:14:45,710
She's mostly here to vent anger.

373
00:14:45,841 --> 00:14:47,669
- Of course I am!

374
00:14:47,799 --> 00:14:49,671
Do you think I could
just let it slide

375
00:14:49,801 --> 00:14:51,238
that my little niece
is going to

376
00:14:51,368 --> 00:14:52,848
find a husband
before I do?

377
00:14:52,979 --> 00:14:54,197
I mean, come on!

378
00:14:54,328 --> 00:14:56,199
She's 900 years
younger than me!

379
00:14:56,330 --> 00:14:57,722
I can't accept this!

380
00:14:57,853 --> 00:14:59,159
It's ridiculous!

381
00:14:59,289 --> 00:15:00,638
Don't you agree?

382
00:15:00,769 --> 00:15:02,553
- It's fine if you
wanna come play,

383
00:15:02,684 --> 00:15:05,905
but you shouldn't be causing
problems for other people.

384
00:15:06,035 --> 00:15:07,254
And it goes without saying that

385
00:15:07,384 --> 00:15:09,909
you're going to clean up
this mess, right?

386
00:15:13,347 --> 00:15:14,522
- [Hakuren] So you two
are always getting

387
00:15:14,652 --> 00:15:16,263
to eat food that
tastes this good?

388
00:15:16,393 --> 00:15:19,135
- Well, it's not like I'm always
imposing on everyone here.

389
00:15:19,266 --> 00:15:21,181
Only three out of
every ten days.

390
00:15:21,311 --> 00:15:22,051
- Oh wow!

391
00:15:22,182 --> 00:15:23,748
Lucky you!

392
00:15:23,879 --> 00:15:25,228
- Maybe it's five days.
- She's already fitting in.

393
00:15:25,359 --> 00:15:27,100
- [Hakuren] Five days?
- Mayor.

394
00:15:27,230 --> 00:15:29,667
I'm sorry about what happened
and that my aunt is...

395
00:15:29,798 --> 00:15:31,191
- [Hakuren] Hey, Lasty!

396
00:15:31,321 --> 00:15:34,063
- That Big Sis Hakuren
is causing so much trouble.

397
00:15:34,194 --> 00:15:37,197
- It's nothing you need
to apologize about.

398
00:15:37,327 --> 00:15:38,938
- Oh, hey!

399
00:15:39,068 --> 00:15:41,114
I heard you have some really
fun games you all play.

400
00:15:41,244 --> 00:15:43,681
Like the one where you line up
the little square things.

401
00:15:43,812 --> 00:15:45,466
- Do you mean mahjong?

402
00:15:45,596 --> 00:15:46,858
- [Hakuren] I wanna try that.

403
00:15:46,989 --> 00:15:48,599
You play with
four people, right?

404
00:15:48,730 --> 00:15:50,732
Hey, mayor!
Let's play a round!

405
00:15:50,862 --> 00:15:53,474
I don't wanna leave here
only having lost to you.

406
00:15:53,604 --> 00:15:55,650
- All right, that's fine by me.

407
00:15:55,780 --> 00:15:58,087
So, first, let me
explain all the rules.

408
00:15:58,218 --> 00:16:00,437
- I'll be fine!
I can figure it out.

409
00:16:00,568 --> 00:16:01,743
- Is that so?

410
00:16:01,873 --> 00:16:04,006
- More importantly...

411
00:16:04,137 --> 00:16:06,008
what should we bet on?

412
00:16:06,139 --> 00:16:06,966
- Huh?

413
00:16:07,096 --> 00:16:07,923
[Dryme chuckling]

414
00:16:08,054 --> 00:16:08,968
- I see, then.

415
00:16:09,098 --> 00:16:10,578
Yes, doing it this way

416
00:16:10,708 --> 00:16:13,233
is more fun than
just playing the game.

417
00:16:13,363 --> 00:16:15,409
- Let's take it easy at first.

418
00:16:15,539 --> 00:16:16,453
- Mayor.

419
00:16:16,584 --> 00:16:17,846
What would you normally bet

420
00:16:17,977 --> 00:16:19,543
when playing mahjong like this?

421
00:16:19,674 --> 00:16:21,676
- Even if want me
to bet something,

422
00:16:21,806 --> 00:16:24,984
I don't really have
anything I can safely bet.

423
00:16:25,114 --> 00:16:26,811
Maybe punish the loser?

424
00:16:26,942 --> 00:16:28,552
The only thing
I can think to do

425
00:16:28,683 --> 00:16:30,032
is play strip mahjong.

426
00:16:30,163 --> 00:16:31,903
[Hakuren squealing]
- Sounds great!

427
00:16:32,034 --> 00:16:34,515
- So the loser gets a
taste of humiliation, then.

428
00:16:34,645 --> 00:16:37,561
- No, no! Don't do anything
you don't want to do!

429
00:16:37,692 --> 00:16:39,128
Right, Lasty?

430
00:16:39,259 --> 00:16:41,696
- If we're competing,
there's no way I can lose.

431
00:16:41,826 --> 00:16:43,089
- [Hiraku] Excuse me?

432
00:16:43,219 --> 00:16:45,178
- [Group] As a member
of the dragon clan!

433
00:16:45,308 --> 00:16:46,396
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
I have a feeling

434
00:16:46,527 --> 00:16:48,659
that things are
going to get bad.

435
00:16:53,186 --> 00:16:54,230
- That's chii!

436
00:16:54,361 --> 00:16:55,492
[Dryme gasping]
- That's riichi!

437
00:16:55,623 --> 00:16:56,580
- Too bad.

438
00:16:56,711 --> 00:16:57,538
Ron!

439
00:16:57,668 --> 00:16:58,974
- [Dryme] What?

440
00:16:59,105 --> 00:17:00,323
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
This is my fault

441
00:17:00,454 --> 00:17:02,630
for carelessly
suggesting this idea.

442
00:17:02,760 --> 00:17:04,023
[Dryme grunting]

443
00:17:04,153 --> 00:17:06,503
- This is indeed
a very shameful thing.

444
00:17:06,634 --> 00:17:09,158
- [Hiraku Voiceover] The dragons
are all very competitive

445
00:17:09,289 --> 00:17:11,378
and they can't stand losing.

446
00:17:11,508 --> 00:17:14,555
This lead to a very serious
game of strip mahjong.

447
00:17:14,685 --> 00:17:16,209
You're new to this,
aren't you?

448
00:17:16,339 --> 00:17:18,124
And you're wearing
the least clothing.

449
00:17:18,254 --> 00:17:19,429
How are you so confident?

450
00:17:19,560 --> 00:17:21,257
Now that it's come to this,

451
00:17:21,388 --> 00:17:23,651
I wanted to carefully rack up
some points and end things

452
00:17:23,781 --> 00:17:25,305
while maintaining the peace,
but...

453
00:17:25,435 --> 00:17:28,047
[suspenseful music]
Something isn't right.

454
00:17:28,177 --> 00:17:30,527
Seriously,
what's happening here?

455
00:17:30,658 --> 00:17:31,920
How am I losing?

456
00:17:32,051 --> 00:17:33,661
I'm on my last
piece of clothing!

457
00:17:33,791 --> 00:17:36,794
Don't tell me they're using
some kind of magic trickery!

458
00:17:36,925 --> 00:17:39,232
Are they using telekinesis
to rewrite the tiles?

459
00:17:39,362 --> 00:17:41,712
Can they see through
the back of my tiles?

460
00:17:41,843 --> 00:17:43,062
No.

461
00:17:43,192 --> 00:17:44,759
- Nothing's written on this one.

462
00:17:44,889 --> 00:17:46,195
Is it an extra?

463
00:17:46,326 --> 00:17:48,328
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
I'm overthinking it.

464
00:17:48,458 --> 00:17:50,112
In any case...

465
00:17:51,592 --> 00:17:53,898
my chance has finally arrived.

466
00:17:54,029 --> 00:17:55,726
I can score a double yakuman.

467
00:17:55,857 --> 00:17:58,599
I can end the whole thing
with a single move.

468
00:17:59,513 --> 00:18:00,731
But...

469
00:18:00,862 --> 00:18:03,560
Of course it had to be
this tile again!

470
00:18:04,474 --> 00:18:06,085
It doesn't matter.

471
00:18:06,215 --> 00:18:08,652
I'll never beat the dragons
if I'm paralyzed by fear!

472
00:18:10,089 --> 00:18:11,481
- [Group] Ron!

473
00:18:11,612 --> 00:18:14,005
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
That's about right.

474
00:18:14,136 --> 00:18:15,790
- Okay, pants off!

475
00:18:15,920 --> 00:18:16,791
- [Girls] Pants off!

476
00:18:16,921 --> 00:18:18,009
Pants off!

477
00:18:18,140 --> 00:18:19,010
[Lastismoon gasping]
Pants off!

478
00:18:19,141 --> 00:18:20,882
Pants off! Pants off!

479
00:18:21,012 --> 00:18:22,927
[girls squealing]
- [Hiraku] I am defeated!

480
00:18:23,058 --> 00:18:25,104
[girls squealing]

481
00:18:25,234 --> 00:18:26,714
- [Grattz] The dragons
are gathering

482
00:18:26,844 --> 00:18:28,237
in that village again?

483
00:18:28,368 --> 00:18:29,369
- Yes.

484
00:18:29,499 --> 00:18:31,022
The ancient dragon Hakuren

485
00:18:31,153 --> 00:18:32,894
was spotted
staying there as well.

486
00:18:33,024 --> 00:18:34,504
- Impossible.

487
00:18:34,635 --> 00:18:36,811
They've got enough power
to conquer a whole country!

488
00:18:36,941 --> 00:18:39,379
Can we afford to just
sit back and watch?

489
00:18:39,509 --> 00:18:42,425
- So, more importantly,
Beezel...

490
00:18:42,556 --> 00:18:43,557
- Yes?

491
00:18:43,687 --> 00:18:45,646
Do you have an idea, Galgardo?

492
00:18:45,776 --> 00:18:46,560
- No.

493
00:18:46,690 --> 00:18:47,561
It's my daughter.

494
00:18:47,691 --> 00:18:49,389
She's been in a mood lately.

495
00:18:49,519 --> 00:18:51,608
She hasn't said
anything to me all day

496
00:18:51,739 --> 00:18:53,436
besides good morning.

497
00:18:53,567 --> 00:18:55,395
Is this her rebellious phase?

498
00:18:55,525 --> 00:18:58,833
- Anyways, we need to focus on
preparing our military forces!

499
00:18:58,963 --> 00:19:01,052
We'll have to secure
the funds we need.

500
00:19:01,183 --> 00:19:02,706
- [Randan Voiceover]
I resign. Randan.

501
00:19:02,837 --> 00:19:03,838
- [Grattz] Randan?

502
00:19:03,968 --> 00:19:05,013
- [Beezel] Ah, he ran away.

503
00:19:05,144 --> 00:19:07,755
- [Grattz] Is this a joke?

504
00:19:07,885 --> 00:19:11,672
- So, if you divide these apples
between three people,

505
00:19:11,802 --> 00:19:14,501
how many apples will
you have to eat, then?

506
00:19:14,631 --> 00:19:17,243
I wish I could just
eat them all, though.

507
00:19:17,373 --> 00:19:19,288
[class laughing]

508
00:19:19,419 --> 00:19:21,725
- She's really come
into her own here.

509
00:19:21,856 --> 00:19:23,074
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
After attacking

510
00:19:23,205 --> 00:19:24,554
The Great Tree Village,

511
00:19:24,685 --> 00:19:27,296
Hakuren decided to stay here
for the time being.

512
00:19:27,427 --> 00:19:31,300
Surprisingly, she's very skilled
and able to handle any job.

513
00:19:31,431 --> 00:19:33,868
But she complains about
anything she's asked to do.

514
00:19:33,998 --> 00:19:36,175
Every time I look,
she's doing nothing.

515
00:19:36,305 --> 00:19:37,828
- I don't wanna.

516
00:19:37,959 --> 00:19:40,527
- Why do you complain about
everything so much?

517
00:19:40,657 --> 00:19:42,093
- I'm hoping that one day,

518
00:19:42,224 --> 00:19:43,791
maybe people will stop
asking me to do things.

519
00:19:43,921 --> 00:19:45,096
[Hiraku sighing]

520
00:19:45,227 --> 00:19:46,359
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
I had no choice

521
00:19:46,489 --> 00:19:47,708
but to order her
to start digging holes

522
00:19:47,838 --> 00:19:49,275
and then filling
them back in.

523
00:19:49,405 --> 00:19:51,102
- Stop being so cruel!
- She gave up on day one.

524
00:19:51,233 --> 00:19:52,713
- [Hiraku Voiceover] In the end,

525
00:19:52,843 --> 00:19:54,758
we settled on her teaching
reading, writing, and math.

526
00:19:54,889 --> 00:19:56,282
She became the village teacher.

527
00:19:56,412 --> 00:19:57,848
- And that's why
learning to read, write,

528
00:19:57,979 --> 00:19:59,850
and do math will
end up helping you

529
00:19:59,981 --> 00:20:01,983
a lot in your day
to day lives.

530
00:20:02,113 --> 00:20:03,376
Listen up.

531
00:20:03,506 --> 00:20:04,942
I want all of you
to work really hard

532
00:20:05,073 --> 00:20:07,423
so that one day I don't have
to work anymore, okay?

533
00:20:07,554 --> 00:20:08,772
- [Class] Okay!

534
00:20:08,903 --> 00:20:09,904
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
I think her motivation

535
00:20:10,034 --> 00:20:11,384
might not be the greatest.

536
00:20:14,474 --> 00:20:17,738
- Please, we beg of you
to spare our lives.

537
00:20:18,913 --> 00:20:20,349
- What are you talking about?

538
00:20:20,480 --> 00:20:22,003
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
According to what

539
00:20:22,133 --> 00:20:24,135
the lamia girls were saying,

540
00:20:24,266 --> 00:20:26,834
at some point, the
younger animals decided to

541
00:20:26,964 --> 00:20:30,098
clear a dungeon they found
in the middle of the forest,

542
00:20:30,229 --> 00:20:33,188
forcing the lamia to
quickly flee their homes.

543
00:20:33,319 --> 00:20:35,408
[lamia gasping]
[wolves barking]

544
00:20:35,538 --> 00:20:37,366
They didn't know
what they were doing,

545
00:20:37,497 --> 00:20:39,629
but they still caused
a lot of trouble.

546
00:20:39,760 --> 00:20:41,501
- What should we do?

547
00:20:41,631 --> 00:20:44,199
- They came all the way here
to seek our aid and protection

548
00:20:44,330 --> 00:20:45,809
from having lost their homes.

549
00:20:45,940 --> 00:20:48,203
It would not be proper
to turn them away.

550
00:20:48,334 --> 00:20:49,726
- [Hiraku Voiceover] In the end,

551
00:20:49,857 --> 00:20:51,641
we decided to trade
the precious gems

552
00:20:51,772 --> 00:20:54,296
the lamia mined
for some of our crops.

553
00:20:54,427 --> 00:20:57,952
After that, they went back
to their original homes.

554
00:20:58,082 --> 00:21:01,042
- I'd like it if we could
keep trading from now on.

555
00:21:01,172 --> 00:21:02,261
- Yes!

556
00:21:02,391 --> 00:21:03,610
Just ask us for
whatever you want.

557
00:21:03,740 --> 00:21:05,089
- [Hiraku Voiceover]
They're so genuinely

558
00:21:05,220 --> 00:21:06,830
excited about this
that it's making me awkward.

559
00:21:06,961 --> 00:21:10,051
- Okay, then, I have something
I'd like to request.

560
00:21:10,181 --> 00:21:11,574
- [Junea] Yes?

561
00:21:11,705 --> 00:21:13,402
- It's fine if it's only
when you're visiting,

562
00:21:13,533 --> 00:21:16,187
but I'd appreciate it if you
could put some clothes on.

563
00:21:16,318 --> 00:21:17,972
[dreamy music]

564
00:21:18,102 --> 00:21:19,626
- [Hiraku Voiceover] That might
be part of their culture,

565
00:21:19,756 --> 00:21:23,630
but I really had trouble
not staring.

566
00:21:23,760 --> 00:21:26,459
After that, the lamia formed
the Lamia Delivery Service

567
00:21:26,589 --> 00:21:29,157
and started carrying our
trading goods for us.

568
00:21:29,288 --> 00:21:30,637
With everything said and done,

569
00:21:30,767 --> 00:21:33,466
I'm glad we found
some reliable neighbors.

570
00:21:33,596 --> 00:21:36,686
Between this and the increased
trade with the other areas,

571
00:21:36,817 --> 00:21:39,994
it feels like the village
has reached a new level.

572
00:21:40,124 --> 00:21:41,996
- Since we've increased
the amount of trade,

573
00:21:42,126 --> 00:21:43,563
shall we plant more crops?

574
00:21:43,693 --> 00:21:44,607
- Yeah.

575
00:21:44,738 --> 00:21:49,046
[bright folk music]

576
00:21:51,310 --> 00:21:53,094
[ominous music]

577
00:21:54,704 --> 00:21:56,837
- It appears that village is
indeed amassing military might

578
00:21:56,967 --> 00:21:59,274
and planning something
most dreadful.

579
00:21:59,405 --> 00:22:01,885
- It may be that they're
convincing Flowrem to stay there

580
00:22:02,016 --> 00:22:04,540
just so they can use her as
a hostage if they need to.

581
00:22:04,671 --> 00:22:07,282
- We should begin gathering
our troops at once,

582
00:22:07,413 --> 00:22:08,849
Princess.

583
00:22:10,111 --> 00:22:11,808
- I understand.

584
00:22:11,939 --> 00:22:14,028
We must defeat that village.

585
00:22:14,158 --> 00:22:16,726
And we have to save Flowrem.

586
00:22:17,945 --> 00:22:21,122
["Feel the winds"
by Yui Hizuki plays]

587
00:23:47,469 --> 00:23:50,646
[rustic music playing]

